---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { profile } from '../data/profile';
---
<BaseLayout title="About" description={`Professional biography of ${profile.name} — 18+ years from Java engineering in 2008 to VP Engineering in regulated financial services, now focused on AI-native systems.`} path="/about">
  <article style="max-width: 720px; margin: 0 auto;">
    <p class="eyebrow">About</p>
    <h1 style="font-size: 34px; margin: 8px 0 16px;">{profile.firstName} Chatterjee</h1>
    <p class="hero-serif" style="font-size: 19px; color: var(--color-text-secondary); margin-bottom: 24px;">{profile.shortIntro}</p>
    {profile.longIntro.map((p) => <p style="margin-bottom: 20px;">{p}</p>)}

    <h2 style="font-size: 22px; margin: 36px 0 14px;">The through-line</h2>
    <p style="margin-bottom: 16px;">My career is a steady evolution: hands-on Java and full-stack engineering (2008–2015) → U.S.-based integration and cloud architecture at Qualcomm (2016–2018) → high-throughput risk-platform architecture at L&T Infotech (2018–2019) → multi-layer engineering leadership for Citi’s AML and risk technology (2019–present). At each step I have moved one level up the stack — code, systems, platforms, organisations — while staying accountable for whether the technology actually delivered business outcomes.</p>
    <p style="margin-bottom: 16px;">The regulated context has been a constant. AML/KYC, auditability, and high-security environments demand a different kind of engineering discipline: evidence before commitment, metrics as culture, and platforms that multiply every team’s output. That discipline is what I now bring to AI-native engineering — RAG pipelines and AI-assisted delivery adopted with POC benchmarks and ROI governance, not vendor enthusiasm.</p>

    <h2 style="font-size: 22px; margin: 36px 0 14px;">Current focus</h2>
    <ul style="list-style: disc; padding-left: 24px; color: var(--color-text-secondary);">
      {profile.currentInterests.map((i) => <li style="margin-bottom: 6px;"><strong style="color: var(--color-text);">{i.title}</strong> — {i.note}</li>)}
    </ul>
    <p style="margin-top: 12px;">Open to: {profile.targetRoles.join(' · ')}.</p>

    <h2 style="font-size: 22px; margin: 36px 0 14px;">Engineering leadership philosophy</h2>
    <p style="margin-bottom: 16px;">Great engineering organisations are built through disciplined operating models, not just talent. My consistent focus is on building the machine that builds the product.</p>
    {profile.leadershipPrinciples.map((p) => (
      <div style="border-left: 3px solid var(--color-accent); padding-left: 16px; margin-bottom: 16px;">
        <h3 style="font-size: 16px;">{p.title}</h3>
        <p style="color: var(--color-text-secondary);">{p.note}</p>
      </div>
    ))}

    <h2 style="font-size: 22px; margin: 36px 0 14px;">Connect</h2>
    <p style="display: flex; gap: 16px; flex-wrap: wrap;">
      {profile.socials.map((s) => {
        const isMailto = s.href.startsWith('mailto:');
        const isPlaceholder = s.href.startsWith('TODO(owner)');
        return <a href={isMailto || isPlaceholder ? '#' : s.href} target={isMailto && !isPlaceholder ? '_blank' : undefined} rel={isMailto && !isPlaceholder ? 'noopener noreferrer' : undefined} style="color: var(--color-accent); font-weight: 600;">{s.label} ↗</a>;
      })}
    </p>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
